  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything yet, because removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` conflicts with ARCH-4.\n\n- **The event is a contract with other repos.** `OrderPlaced` (`src/core/events.ts:16`) is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest. ARCH-4 says removals must go through deprecation, not be done in one step. I can't see those repos, so I can't confirm that nothing reads `channel`. A deployed consumer that does would break.\n- **The model and the event are linked.** `orderPlaced()` copies `order.channel` into the event. If I remove `channel` from the order model, the event can't carry a real value any more.\n\nI can see two ways forward:\n\n1. **Deprecate first (my recommendation).**\n   - In this change, mark `channel` as `@deprecated` on `OrderPlaced` and make it optional in the type.\n   - Keep populating it from the order for now, and announce the deprecation to billing-service and analytics-ingest.\n   - Remove it from the event and the model in a later change, once both teams confirm they don't use it.\n2. **Remove it everywhere now.** I'd do this if you can confirm that both consumer teams have signed off and the schema is allowed to drop the field. I'd remove `channel` from:\n   - the order model and `NewOrder`\n   - `CHANNELS` and its validation\n   - request parsing\n   - the event\n   - the tests and docs\n\n   I'd probably bump `schemaVersion` to 4, but I'd want your call on that.\n\nOn the HTTP side, `GET /orders/{id}` doesn't return `channel`, so ARCH-8 isn't affected. If `POST /orders` stops requiring it, clients that still send it would be fine as long as it's ignored.\n\nWhich option do you want?",
